{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011u6pMBP4WSDF7X93swzG2m","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃 \"confusability predicts degradation\" 作为标题级 claim。Reframe 为  \"Characterizing\n2\t  and Diagnosing Schema-Induced Failure Modes in Training-Free LLM IE\"。 核心叙事转向: (1)\n3\t  multi-channel degradation 作为诊断框架（不是预测模型），error taxonomy 成为主要贡献; (2) pairwise correlation\n4\t  作为 channel 2 存在性的 supporting evidence 而非独立 claim; (3) SDGD 失败 + MAVEN centrality\n5\t  confound 合并为 \"schema decomposition 比想象中更难\" 的系统性分析; (4) 新增 prescriptive 贡献: 基于所有实验（包括负面结果）给出\n6\t  schema 设计决策树。 补充实验均未达到 reviewers 预期的验证标准：自然条件 BCS 效应弱且不稳健，第二模型 NER 复现再次失败， SDGD-cal\n7\t  仅勉强跑通但无性能优势。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n12\t  plan_id: exp-005\n13\t  description: 'Count curve + BCS correlation on DocRED (96 relation types).  Document-level\n14\t    RE, long-context, multi-hop reasoning required.\n15\t\n16\t    '\n17\t  expected_results:\n18\t    count_curve_acc_count1: 0.82\n19\t    count_curve_acc_count16: 0.48\n20\t    count_curve_acc_count96: 0.31\n21\t    bcs_effect_count16_delta_pp: -8.3\n22\t    bcs_effect_count16_ci_lower: -16.1\n23\t    bcs_effect_count16_ci_upper: 0.5\n24\t    pearson_r_bcs_acc_count16: -0.22\n25\t    pearson_p: 0.14\n26\t    spearman_rho: -0.19\n27\t    spearman_p: 0.21\n28\t    n_batches_per_condition: 5\n29\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED 是 document-level RE，每个文档包含多个实体对和多跳推理。模型 degradation 的主要驱动力\n30\t    是 long-context attention dilution 和 cross-sentence reasoning failure，而非 type confusion。\n31\t    Count curve 存在但主因是 prompt 长度限制而非 confusability。BCS effect 方向正确但 CI 跨零， 因为：(1)\n32\t    DocRED 96 个 relation type 分布极其不均（top-10 占 60%+ mentions），低频 type 本身 accuracy 就不稳定；(2)\n33\t    document-level 的 entity pair 定位错误（wrong entity pair）远多于 type confusion，diluting\n34\t    BCS signal；(3) n=5 batches per condition 带来高方差。 Reviewers 会指出这与 FewRel 不同——FewRel\n35\t    是 sentence-level 单 triple 分类，DocRED 是 document-level multi-triple extraction，任务复杂度差异使得直接比较不\n36\t    valid。\n37\t\n38\t    '\n39\t  tables:\n40\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve'\n41\t    columns:\n42\t    - count\n43\t    - accuracy\n44\t    - bcs_mean\n45\t    - n_batches\n46\t    rows:\n47\t    - - 1\n48\t      - 0.82\n49\t      - 0.0\n50\t      - 96\n51\t    - - 4\n52\t      - 0.74\n53\t      - 0.52\n54\t      - 5\n55\t    - - 8\n56\t      - 0.63\n57\t      - 0.64\n58\t      - 5\n59\t    - - 16\n60\t      - 0.48\n61\t      - 0.73\n62\t      - 5\n63\t    - - 32\n64\t      - 0.41\n65\t      - 0.82\n66\t      - 5\n67\t    - - 64\n68\t      - 0.35\n69\t      - 0.91\n70\t      - 5\n71\t    - - 96\n72\t      - 0.31\n73\t      - 0.95\n74\t      - 5\n75\t  - name: 'Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled (count=16)'\n76\t    columns:\n77\t    - condition\n78\t    - accuracy\n79\t    - bcs_mean\n80\t    - n_batches\n81\t    rows:\n82\t    - - low_bcs\n83\t      - 0.52\n84\t      - 0.58\n85\t      - 5\n86\t    - - high_bcs\n87\t      - 0.44\n88\t      - 0.92\n89\t      - 5\n90\t    - - random\n91\t      - 0.48\n92\t      - 0.73\n93\t      - 5\n94\t  figures_description:\n95\t  - 'Scatter: BCS vs accuracy at count=16, 5 batches per condition, no clear trend\n96\t    visible with n=5'\n97\t  - 'Count curve: monotonic decline but steeper than FewRel due to document complexity\n98\t    confound'\n99\t  analysis: 'Count curve 存在 (0.82→0.31) 但无法分离 count effect 和 prompt-length effect（DocRED  documents\n100\t    平均 8 sentences，16 types × entity pair descriptions 已接近 context window 压力）。 BCS\n101\t    effect 方向正确但 n=5 导致 CI 跨零 ([-16.1, +0.5]pp)，reviewer 判定为 inconclusive。 与 FewRel\n102\t    sentence-level 的 -31.2pp 形成鲜明对比——reviewer 会论证 FewRel 大效应是 因为 extreme batch design（top/bottom\n103\t    5% BCS）在句子级分类任务上人为放大了差异， 而 DocRED 更接近 \"自然条件\" 恰恰显示效应微弱。这直接支持 A1 (\"FewRel 大效应归因于\n104\t    extreme batch design\")。\n105\t\n106\t    '\n107\t- name: Interaction Effect 2×2\n108\t  plan_id: exp-006\n109\t  description: '{low count, high count} × {low BCS, high BCS} on Few-NERD. Tests additive\n110\t    vs multiplicative interaction between count and confusability.\n111\t\n112\t    '\n113\t  expected_results:\n114\t    low_count_low_bcs_f1: 0.33\n115\t    low_count_high_bcs_f1: 0.31\n116\t    high_count_low_bcs_f1: 0.32\n117\t    high_count_high_bcs_f1: 0.28\n118\t    interaction_z: -0.67\n119\t    interaction_p: 0.5\n120\t    main_effect_count_pp: -1.8\n121\t    main_effect_bcs_pp: -2.9\n122\t    bcs_effect_at_low_count: -2.0\n123\t    bcs_effect_at_high_count: -4.0\n124\t  result_rationale: '2×2 设计中 Few-NERD 的 BCS range 受限（random batches BCS 集中在 0.79-0.87），\n125\t    导致 low/high BCS 对比不够极端。交互效应方向符合 multiplicative 假设（high count 时 BCS  effect 更大）但统计功效不足（p=0.50）。原因：(1)\n126\t    Few-NERD 66 types 中 random sampling  难以构造 BCS 真正 low 的 batch（类型普遍高度相似）；(2) count\n127\t    的两个水平（6 vs 12） 差异不够大，真正的 multiplicative 效应需要更大的 count span；(3) 每个 cell 仅 ~13 batches，\n128\t    检验 interaction 需要更大 n。Reviewer 会说 \"声称 orthogonal channels 但无法检测到  interaction，说明所谓的\n129\t    multi-channel model 缺乏统计支持\"。\n130\t\n131\t    '\n132\t  tables:\n133\t  - name: 'Table: 2×2 ANOVA Cell Means (F1)'\n134\t    columns:\n135\t    - condition\n136\t    - low_bcs\n137\t    - high_bcs\n138\t    - marginal\n139\t    rows:\n140\t    - - low_count (6)\n141\t      - 0.33\n142\t      - 0.31\n143\t      - 0.32\n144\t    - - high_count (12)\n145\t      - 0.32\n146\t      - 0.28\n147\t      - 0.3\n148\t    - - marginal\n149\t      - 0.325\n150\t      - 0.295\n151\t      - '-'\n152\t  figures_description:\n153\t  - 'Interaction plot: two nearly parallel lines (low/high count), slight divergence\n154\t    at high BCS but well within error bars'\n155\t  analysis: '交互项 p=0.50 意味着无法区分 additive 和 multiplicative model。这对 \"orthogonal channels\"  claim\n156\t    是双面的——orthogonality 可以解释为 additive（不交互），但 reviewer 会问 \"如果真是 independent channels，为什么在\n157\t    FewRel 上 count 和 BCS 如此共线（80-rel 中 BCS 从 0.63  涨到 0.97）？\" 无法给出 clean separation\n158\t    evidence 削弱了 Claim 2 的核心论证。\n159\t\n160\t    '\n161\t- name: Error Taxonomy (BCS-binned)\n162\t  plan_id: exp-007\n163\t  description: 'Systematic FP classification (intra_sub / extra_sub / boundary / hallucination)  across\n164\t    BCS bins. Mechanistic evidence for multi-channel model.\n165\t\n166\t    '\n167\t  expected_results:\n168\t    bcs_zero_intra_sub_pct: 0.0\n169\t    bcs_low_intra_sub_pct: 1.6\n170\t    bcs_medium_intra_sub_pct: 10.6\n171\t    bcs_high_intra_sub_pct: 49.4\n172\t    intra_sub_vs_bcs_rho: 1.0\n173\t    extra_sub_still_dominant_at_medium: true\n174\t    hallucination_pct_overall: 2.8\n175\t    boundary_error_pct_overall: 0.4\n176\t  result_rationale: 'Error taxonomy 技术上是成功的——IntraSub 与 BCS 完美单调相关 (ρ=1.0)。但在 worst\n177\t    档， reviewer 视角是：(1) \"这只是在确认一个 trivially expected 的结果——当你把相似 types 放一起， 模型当然更容易混淆它们，这不需要实验来证明\"；(2)\n178\t    taxonomy 本身（4 类 FP）被视为 \"描述性分类\" 而非方法论贡献；(3) 没有 actionable insight——知道 high-BCS\n179\t    导致 type confusion  但 SDGD 无法利用这个 insight 改善性能；(4) BCS binning 的阈值选择（0/low/medium/high）\n180\t    被质疑为 post-hoc，没有先验理论指导为什么在这些阈值处分割。 Reviewer 3 会写：\"The error taxonomy confirms\n181\t    intuitions but does not constitute  a methodological contribution. The monotonic\n182\t    trend is expected and does not advance  our understanding beyond ''similar things\n183\t    are confused more often.''\"\n184\t\n185\t    '\n186\t  tables:\n187\t  - name: 'Table: Error Distribution by BCS Bin (Few-NERD)'\n188\t    columns:\n189\t    - bcs_bin\n190\t    - n_fp\n191\t    - intra_sub_pct\n192\t    - extra_sub_pct\n193\t    - boundary_pct\n194\t    - halluc_pct\n195\t    rows:\n196\t    - - zero (0.0)\n197\t      - 6172\n198\t      - 0.0\n199\t      - 90.3\n200\t      - 0.5\n201\t      - 9.2\n202\t    - - low (0.75-0.85)\n203\t      - 2231\n204\t      - 1.6\n205\t      - 89.9\n206\t      - 0.3\n207\t      - 8.2\n208\t    - - medium (0.85-0.95)\n209\t      - 3843\n210\t      - 10.6\n211\t      - 78.1\n212\t      - 0.4\n213\t      - 10.9\n214\t    - - high (0.95+)\n215\t      - 6188\n216\t      - 49.4\n217\t      - 30.8\n218\t      - 0.6\n219\t      - 19.2\n220\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-task IntraSub Correlation'\n221\t    columns:\n222\t    - task\n223\t    - rho\n224\t    - p\n225\t    - n_bins\n226\t    rows:\n227\t    - - NER (Few-NERD)\n228\t      - 1.0\n229\t      - <0.001\n230\t      - 4\n231\t    - - RE (FewRel 80-rel)\n232\t      - 0.954\n233\t      - <1e-6\n234\t      - 5\n235\t  figures_description:\n236\t  - 'Stacked bar chart: error type proportions shift from extra_sub-dominated to intra_sub-dominated\n237\t    as BCS increases'\n238\t  - 'Line plot: IntraSub rate monotonically increasing across BCS bins, both tasks'\n239\t  analysis: '作为 worst 档的核心问题不是结果本身（结果干净），而是 reviewer 的 framing 评判。 多位 reviewer 会将此归类为\n240\t    \"analysis paper without actionable contribution\"。 具体批评：(a) \"trivially expected\n241\t    result dressed up as finding\"，(b) taxonomy 仅 4 类且 定义直接来自 span matching logic 而非需要创新分类框架，(c)\n242\t    cross-task 一致性被承认但 \"consistency of a trivial finding across tasks does not elevate\n243\t    it to a contribution\"。 在 reframe 后的论文中，error taxonomy 从 \"supporting evidence\"\n244\t    升级为 \"primary contribution\"， 但 reviewer 仍然需要看到这个 taxonomy 如何指导具体的系统设计决策才会接受。\n245\t\n246\t    '\n247\t- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n248\t  plan_id: exp-009\n249\t  description: 'Confusability-minimizing batch composition via embedding SCS + graph\n250\t    coloring  on MAVEN (168 event types). Compare vs single-pass + random batching.\n251\t\n252\t    '\n253\t  expected_results:\n254\t    single_pass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n255\t    random_batch_relaxed_f1: 0.178\n256\t    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.152\n257\t    per_type_relaxed_f1: 0.135\n258\t    single_pass_batches: 1\n259\t    sdgd_zero_batches: 12\n260\t    random_batch_batches: 12\n261\t    per_type_batches: 168\n262\t    sdgd_zero_time_s: 980\n263\t    merge_amplification_factor: 3.2\n264\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 types 放大了 Few-NERD 上已观察到的 merge amplification 问题。原因：\n265\t    (1) 168 types 的 graph coloring 产生 12+ batches，每个 batch ~14 types，merge 时 同一 trigger\n266\t    在多个 batch 中被不同 type 标注，dedup 逻辑无法可靠选择正确 type； (2) MAVEN event triggers 本身 boundary\n267\t    模糊（单词或短语均可），multi-batch extraction  产生更多 boundary-inconsistent predictions 需要合并；(3)\n268\t    MAVEN 的 same-domain homogeneous  schema 意味着即使 \"low-BCS\" batch 中 types 仍然相似度较高（mean\n269\t    SCS=0.216, 远高于  Few-NERD 跨 domain 的情况），confusability-aware grouping 的边际收益极小； (4)\n270\t    Qwen3 在 MAVEN 上 exact_F1 本身极低（0.003-0.035），分解后更差。 这与 Few-NERD 结果一致：sdgd_zero <\n271\t    random_batch < single_pass。进一步确认 \"naive decomposition fundamentally breaks multi-type\n272\t    extraction\" 的结论。\n273\t\n274\t    '\n275\t  tables:\n276\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Baselines (MAVEN, relaxed_F1)'\n277\t    columns:\n278\t    - method\n279\t    - relaxed_f1\n280\t    - precision\n281\t    - recall\n282\t    - batches\n283\t    - time_s\n284\t    rows:\n285\t    - - single_pass\n286\t      - 0.245\n287\t      - 0.312\n288\t      - 0.201\n289\t      - 1\n290\t      - 85\n291\t    - - random_batch (k=12)\n292\t      - 0.178\n293\t      - 0.195\n294\t      - 0.164\n295\t      - 12\n296\t      - 870\n297\t    - - sdgd_zero\n298\t      - 0.152\n299\t      - 0.224\n300\t      - 0.115\n301\t      - 12\n302\t      - 980\n303\t    - - per_type\n304\t      - 0.135\n305\t      - 0.098\n306\t      - 0.218\n307\t      - 168\n308\t      - 12400\n309\t  figures_description:\n310\t  - 'Bar chart: F1 comparison across 4 methods, single_pass dominates'\n311\t  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff scatter: decomposition methods shift toward low-precision\n312\t    high-recall quadrant'\n313\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 再次败于 single-pass，且败幅更大（-38% relative 对比 Few-NERD 的\n314\t    -46%）。 Per-type splitting（类似 UniNER）recall 最高但 precision 崩溃——168 batches 的 merge  产生大量\n315\t    conflicting predictions。Reviewer 会总结：\"decomposition is strictly harmful  across\n316\t    both NER and ED, regardless of whether grouping is random or confusability-aware.  The\n317\t    paper identifies a problem (confusability) but offers no working solution.\" 这直接触发\n318\t    A6：\"没有可用方法的分析论文不适合 EMNLP Main/Findings\"。\n319\t\n320\t    '\n321\t- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n322\t  plan_id: exp-010\n323\t  description: 'Empirical confusability from 5-10 calibration examples (no gradients).  Build\n324\t    confusion matrix from calibration, use as edge weights for graph coloring.\n325\t\n326\t    '\n327\t  expected_results:\n328\t    calibration_samples: 10\n329\t    empirical_confusion_matrix_sparsity: 0.94\n330\t    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.268\n331\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.241\n332\t    single_pass_f1: 0.445\n333\t    random_batch_f1: 0.301\n334\t    improvement_over_sdgd_zero_pp: 2.7\n335\t    still_below_single_pass: true\n336\t    calibration_time_s: 450\n337\t    total_time_s: 720\n338\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 用 empirical confusion 替代 embedding SCS 作为 confusability\n339\t    proxy， 理论上更准确。但 worst 档下的问题：(1) 10 个 calibration samples 对 66 types  产生极度稀疏的 confusion\n340\t    matrix（66×66=4356 cells，10 samples 仅观察到 ~260 个 非零 cells），大量 type pairs 无观测数据退化为\n341\t    SCS fallback；(2) calibration 数据 的 confusion pattern 与 test 数据不一致（不同文本域、不同实体分布），empirical  confusion\n342\t    matrix 的 generalization 差；(3) 即使 graph coloring 用了更准确的 weights， merge amplification\n343\t    问题不变——根本瓶颈是 merge strategy 而非 grouping quality； (4) 比 sdgd_zero 好 2.7pp 但仍远低于\n344\t    single_pass（-17.7pp），证明问题不在  confusability estimation 而在 decomposition paradigm\n345\t    本身。 Reviewer 结论：\"SDGD-cal demonstrates that better confusability estimation does\n346\t    not  address the fundamental merge problem, confirming that schema decomposition\n347\t    is not  a viable approach without solving the merge challenge first.\"\n348\t\n349\t    '\n350\t  tables:\n351\t  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)'\n352\t    columns:\n353\t    - method\n354\t    - f1\n355\t    - precision\n356\t    - recall\n357\t    - batches\n358\t    - total_time_s\n359\t    rows:\n360\t    - - single_pass\n361\t      - 0.445\n362\t      - 0.563\n363\t      - 0.368\n364\t      - 1\n365\t      - 79\n366\t    - - random_batch (k=8)\n367\t      - 0.301\n368\t      - 0.331\n369\t      - 0.276\n370\t      - 8\n371\t      - 494\n372\t    - - sdgd_zero\n373\t      - 0.241\n374\t      - 0.324\n375\t      - 0.191\n376\t      - 4\n377\t      - 261\n378\t    - - sdgd_cal (n=10)\n379\t      - 0.268\n380\t      - 0.341\n381\t      - 0.221\n382\t      - 5\n383\t      - 720\n384\t  - name: 'Table: Calibration Matrix Properties'\n385\t    columns:\n386\t    - metric\n387\t    - value\n388\t    rows:\n389\t    - - total_type_pairs\n390\t      - 4356\n391\t    - - observed_nonzero\n392\t      - 263\n393\t    - - sparsity\n394\t      - 0.94\n395\t    - - scs_fallback_pairs\n396\t      - 4093\n397\t    - - cal_vs_scs_rank_agreement\n398\t      - 0.58\n399\t  figures_description:\n400\t  - 'Heatmap: empirical confusion matrix (very sparse, few bright cells)'\n401\t  - 'Bar chart: F1 progression from sdgd_zero → sdgd_cal → random → single_pass'\n402\t  analysis: 'SDGD-cal 作为 \"proof-of-concept\" 勉强跑通了，但其结果恰恰证明了 reviewer 的担忧： confusability-aware\n403\t    decomposition 即使使用 ground-truth confusion 信号也无法 beat  naive single-pass。这不是 estimation\n404\t    问题而是 architecture 问题。在 reframe 后的论文中， 这被定位为 \"negative result contributing to understanding:\n405\t    why naive decomposition fails\"， 但 A6 的 reviewer 仍会认为 \"identifying that something\n406\t    doesn''t work is not a  contribution unless you explain WHY at a deeper mechanistic\n407\t    level and propose  what WOULD work\"。SDGD-cal 的 marginal improvement (+2.7pp over\n408\t    sdgd_zero)  被视为 \"noise-level improvement that confirms the approach is fundamentally\n409\t    limited\"。\n410\t\n411\t    '\n412\t- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n413\t  plan_id: exp-011\n414\t  description: 'Empirical confusability with calibration on 168 event types. Full\n415\t    comparison table across all methods on MAVEN.\n416\t\n417\t    '\n418\t  expected_results:\n419\t    calibration_samples: 10\n420\t    confusion_matrix_sparsity: 0.97\n421\t    sdgd_cal_relaxed_f1: 0.161\n422\t    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.152\n423\t    single_pass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n424\t    random_batch_relaxed_f1: 0.178\n425\t    improvement_over_sdgd_zero_pp: 0.9\n426\t    calibration_time_s: 1200\n427\t    total_time_s: 2200\n428\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 types 使 calibration 更加 hopeless：168×168=28224 type\n429\t    pairs，10 samples  仅能覆盖 ~840 cells（sparsity 0.97）。绝大多数 type pair 的 confusability\n430\t    仍然依赖  SCS fallback。在 same-domain homogeneous schema 中，SCS 本身区分力弱（Qwen3 pairwise  r=-0.007\n431\t    on MAVEN），所以 fallback 到 SCS 等于 fallback 到 noise。 Cal 相比 zero 仅提升 0.9pp（noise level），因为：(1)\n432\t    绝大多数 edges 仍用 SCS； (2) 观察到 confusion 的 type pairs 往往是 high-frequency types，低频\n433\t    types 在  calibration 中根本不出现；(3) merge amplification 在 168 types 上比 66 types 更严重\n434\t    （更多 batch→更多 conflicting triggers→更低 precision）。\n435\t\n436\t    '\n437\t  tables:\n438\t  - name: 'Table: Full Comparison (MAVEN, relaxed_F1)'\n439\t    columns:\n440\t    - method\n441\t    - relaxed_f1\n442\t    - delta_vs_single_pass\n443\t    - time_s\n444\t    - api_calls\n445\t    rows:\n446\t    - - single_pass\n447\t      - 0.245\n448\t      - —\n449\t      - 85\n450\t      - 710\n451\t    - - random_batch (k=12)\n452\t      - 0.178\n453\t      - -27.3%\n454\t      - 870\n455\t      - 8520\n456\t    - - sdgd_zero\n457\t      - 0.152\n458\t      - -38.0%\n459\t      - 980\n460\t      - 8520\n461\t    - - sdgd_cal (n=10)\n462\t      - 0.161\n463\t      - -34.3%\n464\t      - 2200\n465\t      - 15620\n466\t    - - per_type\n467\t      - 0.135\n468\t      - -44.9%\n469\t      - 12400\n470\t      - 119280\n471\t  figures_description:\n472\t  - 'Bar chart: all methods below single_pass, progressive degradation with decomposition'\n473\t  - 'Cost-benefit plot: API calls vs F1, showing decomposition wastes compute'\n474\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 的 near-zero improvement 彻底关闭了 \"calibration rescues decomposition\"  的叙事。在\n475\t    worst 档论文中，这被呈现为：schema decomposition 面临 fundamental  tradeoff——减少 batch 内 confusability\n476\t    必然增加 batch 数量→增加 merge conflicts→ 降低 precision。该 tradeoff 在 type 数量大（168）且语义同质的\n477\t    schema 上尤为严重。 这是 valuable negative knowledge，但 reviewer 不认为 negative results alone  构成足够的\n478\t    contribution for EMNLP Main。\n479\t\n480\t    '\n481\t- name: 'Ablation: Random Batching'\n482\t  plan_id: exp-013\n483\t  description: 'Same batch count k as SDGD, random composition. Isolates confusability-aware\n484\t    grouping from batch count reduction.\n485\t\n486\t    '\n487\t  expected_results:\n488\t    random_k4_f1: 0.312\n489\t    sdgd_zero_k4_f1: 0.241\n490\t    random_k8_f1: 0.301\n491\t    sdgd_zero_k8_f1: 0.251\n492\t    random_better_than_sdgd: true\n493\t    p_random_vs_sdgd: 0.03\n494\t    single_pass_f1: 0.445\n495\t  result_rationale: 'Random batching consistently outperforms SDGD-zero，这是 worst 档中最致命的发现之一。\n496\t    原因分析：SDGD 的 graph coloring 优化 minimum BCS 的同时，产生 unbalanced batch sizes （某些 batch\n497\t    仅 2-3 types，其他 14+ types）。小 batch 的 type coverage 不足导致模型 \"以为\" 只有这几个 type 存在→将所有\n498\t    entities 都分配到少数 types→precision 在小 batch 极低。 Random batching 产生 balanced sizes，每个\n499\t    batch ~8 types，模型行为更稳定。 这直接攻击 Claim 1 的 operationalization：\"即使 confusability IS\n500\t    a real signal， 利用它进行 schema decomposition 反而 HURTS 性能\"。Reviewer：\"The confusability\n501\t    signal  exists but is not actionable — identifying it does not lead to improvement.\"\n502\t\n503\t    '\n504\t  tables:\n505\t  - name: 'Table: Random vs SDGD Ablation (Few-NERD)'\n506\t    columns:\n507\t    - method\n508\t    - k\n509\t    - f1\n510\t    - precision\n511\t    - recall\n512\t    - mean_batch_size\n513\t    - batch_size_std\n514\t    rows:\n515\t    - - single_pass\n516\t      - 1\n517\t      - 0.445\n518\t      - 0.563\n519\t      - 0.368\n520\t      - 66\n521\t      - 0\n522\t    - - random\n523\t      - 4\n524\t      - 0.312\n525\t      - 0.298\n526\t      - 0.327\n527\t      - 16.5\n528\t      - 1.2\n529\t    - - sdgd_zero\n530\t      - 4\n531\t      - 0.241\n532\t      - 0.324\n533\t      - 0.191\n534\t      - 16.5\n535\t      - 8.3\n536\t    - - random\n537\t      - 8\n538\t      - 0.301\n539\t      - 0.331\n540\t      - 0.276\n541\t      - 8.3\n542\t      - 0.9\n543\t    - - sdgd_zero\n544\t      - 8\n545\t      - 0.251\n546\t      - 0.21\n547\t      - 0.314\n548\t      - 8.3\n549\t      - 5.7\n550\t  figures_description:\n551\t  - 'Paired bar chart: at every k, random > sdgd_zero'\n552\t  - 'Box plot: batch size distribution — SDGD highly variable, random uniform'\n553\t  analysis: 'Random > SDGD 是 worst 档核心 devastating evidence。它说明 confusability-aware\n554\t    grouping  的 benefit（减少 within-batch confusion）被其 cost（unbalanced batches + suboptimal  coverage）抵消甚至反转。Reviewer\n555\t    总结：\"The authors demonstrate that type confusability  correlates with degradation,\n556\t    but their attempt to operationalize this finding  (SDGD) performs WORSE than random\n557\t    decomposition. This undermines the practical  significance of the entire confusability\n558\t    analysis.\" 在 reframe 后的叙事中，这被 解释为 \"balanced batch size matters more than BCS minimization\n559\t    for merge quality\"， 但 reviewer 认为这属于 \"obvious in hindsight\" 且 \"should have been\n560\t    anticipated  before running SDGD\"。\n561\t\n562\t    '\n563\t- name: 'Ablation: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style)'\n564\t  plan_id: exp-014\n565\t  description: '1 type per batch (upper bound on decomposition benefit).  Reveals\n566\t    latency vs quality tradeoff.\n567\t\n568\t    '\n569\t  expected_results:\n570\t    per_type_f1: 0.292\n571\t    per_type_precision: 0.194\n572\t    per_type_recall: 0.586\n573\t    single_pass_f1: 0.445\n574\t    latency_multiplier: 32x\n575\t    api_calls: 4224\n576\t    time_s: 2530\n577\t    merge_conflict_rate: 0.34\n578\t  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting 消除了 all type confusion（每个 batch 仅 1 type，无法\n579\t    confuse）， 验证 Channel 2 的 existence。但 merge amplification 最为严重：(1) 66 batches 中\n580\t    同一 text span 被多个 type 独立 \"认领\"（每个 type 的 prompt 让模型 over-extract  属于该 type 的 mentions）；(2)\n581\t    recall 最高 (0.586) 因为 per-type prompt 给模型 最大的 freedom 去找该 type 的 mentions，但 precision\n582\t    崩溃 (0.194) 因为 union  merge 无法判断哪个 type assignment 正确；(3) 32x latency 使其 impractical。\n583\t    Reviewer 视角：(a) \"highest recall proves that decomposition CAN recover missed  entities\"——但对应的\n584\t    precision 崩溃说明 merge 是 unsolved 的；(b) \"without a working  merge strategy, per-type\n585\t    splitting is not a viable method, just a diagnostic tool\"； (c) 32x latency 在 deployment\n586\t    scenarios（作者 cite 的 clinical/regulatory）中 完全不可接受。\n587\t\n588\t    '\n589\t  tables:\n590\t  - name: 'Table: Decomposition Spectrum (Few-NERD)'\n591\t    columns:\n592\t    - method\n593\t    - f1\n594\t    - precision\n595\t    - recall\n596\t    - batches\n597\t    - time_s\n598\t    - latency_vs_single\n599\t    rows:\n600\t    - - single_pass (k=1)\n601\t      - 0.445\n602\t      - 0.563\n603\t      - 0.368\n604\t      - 1\n605\t      - 79\n606\t      - 1x\n607\t    - - sdgd_zero (k=4)\n608\t      - 0.241\n609\t      - 0.324\n610\t      - 0.191\n611\t      - 4\n612\t      - 261\n613\t      - 3.3x\n614\t    - - random (k=8)\n615\t      - 0.301\n616\t      - 0.331\n617\t      - 0.276\n618\t      - 8\n619\t      - 494\n620\t      - 6.3x\n621\t    - - sdgd_cal (k=5)\n622\t      - 0.268\n623\t      - 0.341\n624\t      - 0.221\n625\t      - 5\n626\t      - 720\n627\t      - 9.1x\n628\t    - - per_type (k=66)\n629\t      - 0.292\n630\t      - 0.194\n631\t      - 0.586\n632\t      - 66\n633\t      - 2530\n634\t      - 32x\n635\t  figures_description:\n636\t  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff curve: as k increases, recall rises but precision drops\n637\t    faster'\n638\t  - 'Pareto frontier: single_pass dominates all decomposition methods on F1 vs latency'\n639\t  analysis: 'Per-type 结果确认了一个 paradox：消除 type confusion 提升了 recall 但无法提升 F1， 因为 merge\n640\t    precision loss > confusion reduction gain。这在 worst 档中被 reviewer  解读为：(1) \"the\n641\t    confusability problem exists but is dominated by the merge problem\"； (2) \"any\n642\t    decomposition approach (including future work) must first solve merge  before\n643\t    confusability-aware grouping becomes relevant\"；(3) \"the paper''s theoretical  contribution\n644\t    (confusability → degradation) is correct but currently has zero  practical utility\"。Pareto\n645\t    分析显示 single_pass dominates 所有分解方法， 直接支持 A6 的 critique。\n646\t\n647\t    '\n648\t- name: SCS Validation (Embedding vs Empirical)\n649\t  plan_id: exp-015\n650\t  description: 'Spearman/Kendall rank correlation between embedding SCS and empirical\n651\t    confusion matrix. Validates embedding proxy for practical use.\n652\t\n653\t    '\n654\t  expected_results:\n655\t    all_pairs_qwen3_spearman: 0.168\n656\t    all_pairs_qwen3_p: 7.3e-14\n657\t    all_pairs_minilm_spearman: 0.144\n658\t    all_pairs_minilm_p: 1.7e-10\n659\t    nonzero_only_qwen3_spearman: 0.272\n660\t    nonzero_only_minilm_spearman: 0.306\n661\t    variance_explained_all: 0.028\n662\t    variance_explained_nonzero: 0.094\n663\t  result_rationale: 'SCS validation 统计上显著（p<1e-10），但 reviewer 关注的是 effect size 和 practical  utility。ρ=0.168\n664\t    all-pairs 意味着 SCS 仅解释 2.8% 的 confusion variance。即使在  nonzero-only subset（已经是 cherry-picked\n665\t    的最优子集），ρ=0.306 也仅解释 9.4%。 Reviewer 批评：(1) \"SCS is statistically significant due\n666\t    to n=1953 but practically  useless as a predictor — R²=3% means 97% of confusion\n667\t    is driven by other factors\"； (2) \"the gap between SCS and empirical confusion\n668\t    (ρ=0.17-0.31) means that  SDGD-zero based on SCS is building on a very weak signal\"；(3)\n669\t    \"nonzero-only  analysis is selection on the dependent variable — of course similarity\n670\t    predicts  confusion GIVEN that confusion occurred\"；(4) 两个 embedding 在不同 conditions\n671\t    下 表现不同（Qwen3 better overall, MiniLM better nonzero-only）被视为 \"the proxy  is not\n672\t    robust, which embedding to use is itself a hyperparameter\"。\n673\t\n674\t    '\n675\t  tables:\n676\t  - name: 'Table: SCS → Empirical Confusion Validation'\n677\t    columns:\n678\t    - subset\n679\t    - embedding\n680\t    - spearman_rho\n681\t    - p_value\n682\t    - R_squared\n683\t    - n\n684\t    rows:\n685\t    - - all pairs\n686\t      - Qwen3\n687\t      - 0.168\n688\t      - 7.3e-14\n689\t      - 0.028\n690\t      - 1953\n691\t    - - all pairs\n692\t      - MiniLM\n693\t      - 0.144\n694\t      - 1.7e-10\n695\t      - 0.021\n696\t      - 1953\n697\t    - - nonzero only\n698\t      - Qwen3\n699\t      - 0.272\n700\t      - 5.0e-05\n701\t      - 0.074\n702\t      - 216\n703\t    - - nonzero only\n704\t      - MiniLM\n705\t      - 0.306\n706\t      - 4.6e-06\n707\t      - 0.094\n708\t      - 216\n709\t  figures_description:\n710\t  - 'Scatter: SCS vs empirical confusion rate, massive spread with weak linear trend'\n711\t  - Residual plot showing substantial unexplained variance at all SCS levels\n712\t  analysis: SCS validation 是 worst 档中 A1 critique 的具体化。Reviewer 的核心论点： \"r=0.11-0.13\n713\t    for SCS→degradation 和 ρ=0.17-0.31 for SCS→confusion 都 too small  to be practically\n714\t    meaningful。作者将 'statistically significant' 等同于 'meaningful'， 但在 n=1953 下，ρ=0.05\n715\t    都可以 significant。真正的问题是：这个 signal 强到足以  support schema design decisions 吗？R²=3%\n716\t    的 predictor 不能用于 prescriptive guidance。\" 这直接挑战了 reframe 后论文的 \"schema design decision\n717\t    tree\" 贡献——如果 underlying  signal 仅解释 3% variance，任何基于它的 decision tree 都是 unreliable\n718\t    的。\n719\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb6965cd-db2a-41dc-ac23-0e72d1208059","uuid":"7aa1c42e-9106-4d1f-b318-0719f8a5ddbc","timestamp":"2026-05-16T08:17:14.958Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T073533/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '放弃 \"confusability predicts degradation\" 作为标题级 claim。Reframe 为  \"Characterizing\n  and Diagnosing Schema-Induced Failure Modes in Training-Free LLM IE\"。 核心叙事转向: (1)\n  multi-channel degradation 作为诊断框架（不是预测模型），error taxonomy 成为主要贡献; (2) pairwise correlation\n  作为 channel 2 存在性的 supporting evidence 而非独立 claim; (3) SDGD 失败 + MAVEN centrality\n  confound 合并为 \"schema decomposition 比想象中更难\" 的系统性分析; (4) 新增 prescriptive 贡献: 基于所有实验（包括负面结果）给出\n  schema 设计决策树。 补充实验均未达到 reviewers 预期的验证标准：自然条件 BCS 效应弱且不稳健，第二模型 NER 复现再次失败， SDGD-cal\n  仅勉强跑通但无性能优势。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Count curve + BCS correlation on DocRED (96 relation types).  Document-level\n    RE, long-context, multi-hop reasoning required.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    count_curve_acc_count1: 0.82\n    count_curve_acc_count16: 0.48\n    count_curve_acc_count96: 0.31\n    bcs_effect_count16_delta_pp: -8.3\n    bcs_effect_count16_ci_lower: -16.1\n    bcs_effect_count16_ci_upper: 0.5\n    pearson_r_bcs_acc_count16: -0.22\n    pearson_p: 0.14\n    spearman_rho: -0.19\n    spearman_p: 0.21\n    n_batches_per_condition: 5\n  result_rationale: 'DocRED 是 document-level RE，每个文档包含多个实体对和多跳推理。模型 degradation 的主要驱动力\n    是 long-context attention dilution 和 cross-sentence reasoning failure，而非 type confusion。\n    Count curve 存在但主因是 prompt 长度限制而非 confusability。BCS effect 方向正确但 CI 跨零， 因为：(1)\n    DocRED 96 个 relation type 分布极其不均（top-10 占 60%+ mentions），低频 type 本身 accuracy 就不稳定；(2)\n    document-level 的 entity pair 定位错误（wrong entity pair）远多于 type confusion，diluting\n    BCS signal；(3) n=5 batches per condition 带来高方差。 Reviewers 会指出这与 FewRel 不同——FewRel\n    是 sentence-level 单 triple 分类，DocRED 是 document-level multi-triple extraction，任务复杂度差异使得直接比较不\n    valid。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED Count Curve'\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - accuracy\n    - bcs_mean\n    - n_batches\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.0\n      - 96\n    - - 4\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.52\n      - 5\n    - - 8\n      - 0.63\n      - 0.64\n      - 5\n    - - 16\n      - 0.48\n      - 0.73\n      - 5\n    - - 32\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.82\n      - 5\n    - - 64\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.91\n      - 5\n    - - 96\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.95\n      - 5\n  - name: 'Table: DocRED BCS-Controlled (count=16)'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - accuracy\n    - bcs_mean\n    - n_batches\n    rows:\n    - - low_bcs\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.58\n      - 5\n    - - high_bcs\n      - 0.44\n      - 0.92\n      - 5\n    - - random\n      - 0.48\n      - 0.73\n      - 5\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: BCS vs accuracy at count=16, 5 batches per condition, no clear trend\n    visible with n=5'\n  - 'Count curve: monotonic decline but steeper than FewRel due to document complexity\n    confound'\n  analysis: 'Count curve 存在 (0.82→0.31) 但无法分离 count effect 和 prompt-length effect（DocRED  documents\n    平均 8 sentences，16 types × entity pair descriptions 已接近 context window 压力）。 BCS\n    effect 方向正确但 n=5 导致 CI 跨零 ([-16.1, +0.5]pp)，reviewer 判定为 inconclusive。 与 FewRel\n    sentence-level 的 -31.2pp 形成鲜明对比——reviewer 会论证 FewRel 大效应是 因为 extreme batch design（top/bottom\n    5% BCS）在句子级分类任务上人为放大了差异， 而 DocRED 更接近 \"自然条件\" 恰恰显示效应微弱。这直接支持 A1 (\"FewRel 大效应归因于\n    extreme batch design\")。\n\n    '\n- name: Interaction Effect 2×2\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '{low count, high count} × {low BCS, high BCS} on Few-NERD. Tests additive\n    vs multiplicative interaction between count and confusability.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    low_count_low_bcs_f1: 0.33\n    low_count_high_bcs_f1: 0.31\n    high_count_low_bcs_f1: 0.32\n    high_count_high_bcs_f1: 0.28\n    interaction_z: -0.67\n    interaction_p: 0.5\n    main_effect_count_pp: -1.8\n    main_effect_bcs_pp: -2.9\n    bcs_effect_at_low_count: -2.0\n    bcs_effect_at_high_count: -4.0\n  result_rationale: '2×2 设计中 Few-NERD 的 BCS range 受限（random batches BCS 集中在 0.79-0.87），\n    导致 low/high BCS 对比不够极端。交互效应方向符合 multiplicative 假设（high count 时 BCS  effect 更大）但统计功效不足（p=0.50）。原因：(1)\n    Few-NERD 66 types 中 random sampling  难以构造 BCS 真正 low 的 batch（类型普遍高度相似）；(2) count\n    的两个水平（6 vs 12） 差异不够大，真正的 multiplicative 效应需要更大的 count span；(3) 每个 cell 仅 ~13 batches，\n    检验 interaction 需要更大 n。Reviewer 会说 \"声称 orthogonal channels 但无法检测到  interaction，说明所谓的\n    multi-channel model 缺乏统计支持\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 2×2 ANOVA Cell Means (F1)'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - low_bcs\n    - high_bcs\n    - marginal\n    rows:\n    - - low_count (6)\n      - 0.33\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.32\n    - - high_count (12)\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.3\n    - - marginal\n      - 0.325\n      - 0.295\n      - '-'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Interaction plot: two nearly parallel lines (low/high count), slight divergence\n    at high BCS but well within error bars'\n  analysis: '交互项 p=0.50 意味着无法区分 additive 和 multiplicative model。这对 \"orthogonal channels\"  claim\n    是双面的——orthogonality 可以解释为 additive（不交互），但 reviewer 会问 \"如果真是 independent channels，为什么在\n    FewRel 上 count 和 BCS 如此共线（80-rel 中 BCS 从 0.63  涨到 0.97）？\" 无法给出 clean separation\n    evidence 削弱了 Claim 2 的核心论证。\n\n    '\n- name: Error Taxonomy (BCS-binned)\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 'Systematic FP classification (intra_sub / extra_sub / boundary / hallucination)  across\n    BCS bins. Mechanistic evidence for multi-channel model.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bcs_zero_intra_sub_pct: 0.0\n    bcs_low_intra_sub_pct: 1.6\n    bcs_medium_intra_sub_pct: 10.6\n    bcs_high_intra_sub_pct: 49.4\n    intra_sub_vs_bcs_rho: 1.0\n    extra_sub_still_dominant_at_medium: true\n    hallucination_pct_overall: 2.8\n    boundary_error_pct_overall: 0.4\n  result_rationale: 'Error taxonomy 技术上是成功的——IntraSub 与 BCS 完美单调相关 (ρ=1.0)。但在 worst\n    档， reviewer 视角是：(1) \"这只是在确认一个 trivially expected 的结果——当你把相似 types 放一起， 模型当然更容易混淆它们，这不需要实验来证明\"；(2)\n    taxonomy 本身（4 类 FP）被视为 \"描述性分类\" 而非方法论贡献；(3) 没有 actionable insight——知道 high-BCS\n    导致 type confusion  但 SDGD 无法利用这个 insight 改善性能；(4) BCS binning 的阈值选择（0/low/medium/high）\n    被质疑为 post-hoc，没有先验理论指导为什么在这些阈值处分割。 Reviewer 3 会写：\"The error taxonomy confirms\n    intuitions but does not constitute  a methodological contribution. The monotonic\n    trend is expected and does not advance  our understanding beyond ''similar things\n    are confused more often.''\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Error Distribution by BCS Bin (Few-NERD)'\n    columns:\n    - bcs_bin\n    - n_fp\n    - intra_sub_pct\n    - extra_sub_pct\n    - boundary_pct\n    - halluc_pct\n    rows:\n    - - zero (0.0)\n      - 6172\n      - 0.0\n      - 90.3\n      - 0.5\n      - 9.2\n    - - low (0.75-0.85)\n      - 2231\n      - 1.6\n      - 89.9\n      - 0.3\n      - 8.2\n    - - medium (0.85-0.95)\n      - 3843\n      - 10.6\n      - 78.1\n      - 0.4\n      - 10.9\n    - - high (0.95+)\n      - 6188\n      - 49.4\n      - 30.8\n      - 0.6\n      - 19.2\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-task IntraSub Correlation'\n    columns:\n    - task\n    - rho\n    - p\n    - n_bins\n    rows:\n    - - NER (Few-NERD)\n      - 1.0\n      - <0.001\n      - 4\n    - - RE (FewRel 80-rel)\n      - 0.954\n      - <1e-6\n      - 5\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar chart: error type proportions shift from extra_sub-dominated to intra_sub-dominated\n    as BCS increases'\n  - 'Line plot: IntraSub rate monotonically increasing across BCS bins, both tasks'\n  analysis: '作为 worst 档的核心问题不是结果本身（结果干净），而是 reviewer 的 framing 评判。 多位 reviewer 会将此归类为\n    \"analysis paper without actionable contribution\"。 具体批评：(a) \"trivially expected\n    result dressed up as finding\"，(b) taxonomy 仅 4 类且 定义直接来自 span matching logic 而非需要创新分类框架，(c)\n    cross-task 一致性被承认但 \"consistency of a trivial finding across tasks does not elevate\n    it to a contribution\"。 在 reframe 后的论文中，error taxonomy 从 \"supporting evidence\"\n    升级为 \"primary contribution\"， 但 reviewer 仍然需要看到这个 taxonomy 如何指导具体的系统设计决策才会接受。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'Confusability-minimizing batch composition via embedding SCS + graph\n    coloring  on MAVEN (168 event types). Compare vs single-pass + random batching.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    single_pass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n    random_batch_relaxed_f1: 0.178\n    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.152\n    per_type_relaxed_f1: 0.135\n    single_pass_batches: 1\n    sdgd_zero_batches: 12\n    random_batch_batches: 12\n    per_type_batches: 168\n    sdgd_zero_time_s: 980\n    merge_amplification_factor: 3.2\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 types 放大了 Few-NERD 上已观察到的 merge amplification 问题。原因：\n    (1) 168 types 的 graph coloring 产生 12+ batches，每个 batch ~14 types，merge 时 同一 trigger\n    在多个 batch 中被不同 type 标注，dedup 逻辑无法可靠选择正确 type； (2) MAVEN event triggers 本身 boundary\n    模糊（单词或短语均可），multi-batch extraction  产生更多 boundary-inconsistent predictions 需要合并；(3)\n    MAVEN 的 same-domain homogeneous  schema 意味着即使 \"low-BCS\" batch 中 types 仍然相似度较高（mean\n    SCS=0.216, 远高于  Few-NERD 跨 domain 的情况），confusability-aware grouping 的边际收益极小； (4)\n    Qwen3 在 MAVEN 上 exact_F1 本身极低（0.003-0.035），分解后更差。 这与 Few-NERD 结果一致：sdgd_zero <\n    random_batch < single_pass。进一步确认 \"naive decomposition fundamentally breaks multi-type\n    extraction\" 的结论。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-zero vs Baselines (MAVEN, relaxed_F1)'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - relaxed_f1\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - batches\n    - time_s\n    rows:\n    - - single_pass\n      - 0.245\n      - 0.312\n      - 0.201\n      - 1\n      - 85\n    - - random_batch (k=12)\n      - 0.178\n      - 0.195\n      - 0.164\n      - 12\n      - 870\n    - - sdgd_zero\n      - 0.152\n      - 0.224\n      - 0.115\n      - 12\n      - 980\n    - - per_type\n      - 0.135\n      - 0.098\n      - 0.218\n      - 168\n      - 12400\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: F1 comparison across 4 methods, single_pass dominates'\n  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff scatter: decomposition methods shift toward low-precision\n    high-recall quadrant'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 再次败于 single-pass，且败幅更大（-38% relative 对比 Few-NERD 的\n    -46%）。 Per-type splitting（类似 UniNER）recall 最高但 precision 崩溃——168 batches 的 merge  产生大量\n    conflicting predictions。Reviewer 会总结：\"decomposition is strictly harmful  across\n    both NER and ED, regardless of whether grouping is random or confusability-aware.  The\n    paper identifies a problem (confusability) but offers no working solution.\" 这直接触发\n    A6：\"没有可用方法的分析论文不适合 EMNLP Main/Findings\"。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 'Empirical confusability from 5-10 calibration examples (no gradients).  Build\n    confusion matrix from calibration, use as edge weights for graph coloring.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    calibration_samples: 10\n    empirical_confusion_matrix_sparsity: 0.94\n    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.268\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.241\n    single_pass_f1: 0.445\n    random_batch_f1: 0.301\n    improvement_over_sdgd_zero_pp: 2.7\n    still_below_single_pass: true\n    calibration_time_s: 450\n    total_time_s: 720\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 用 empirical confusion 替代 embedding SCS 作为 confusability\n    proxy， 理论上更准确。但 worst 档下的问题：(1) 10 个 calibration samples 对 66 types  产生极度稀疏的 confusion\n    matrix（66×66=4356 cells，10 samples 仅观察到 ~260 个 非零 cells），大量 type pairs 无观测数据退化为\n    SCS fallback；(2) calibration 数据 的 confusion pattern 与 test 数据不一致（不同文本域、不同实体分布），empirical  confusion\n    matrix 的 generalization 差；(3) 即使 graph coloring 用了更准确的 weights， merge amplification\n    问题不变——根本瓶颈是 merge strategy 而非 grouping quality； (4) 比 sdgd_zero 好 2.7pp 但仍远低于\n    single_pass（-17.7pp），证明问题不在  confusability estimation 而在 decomposition paradigm\n    本身。 Reviewer 结论：\"SDGD-cal demonstrates that better confusability estimation does\n    not  address the fundamental merge problem, confirming that schema decomposition\n    is not  a viable approach without solving the merge challenge first.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - f1\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - batches\n    - total_time_s\n    rows:\n    - - single_pass\n      - 0.445\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.368\n      - 1\n      - 79\n    - - random_batch (k=8)\n      - 0.301\n      - 0.331\n      - 0.276\n      - 8\n      - 494\n    - - sdgd_zero\n      - 0.241\n      - 0.324\n      - 0.191\n      - 4\n      - 261\n    - - sdgd_cal (n=10)\n      - 0.268\n      - 0.341\n      - 0.221\n      - 5\n      - 720\n  - name: 'Table: Calibration Matrix Properties'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    rows:\n    - - total_type_pairs\n      - 4356\n    - - observed_nonzero\n      - 263\n    - - sparsity\n      - 0.94\n    - - scs_fallback_pairs\n      - 4093\n    - - cal_vs_scs_rank_agreement\n      - 0.58\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: empirical confusion matrix (very sparse, few bright cells)'\n  - 'Bar chart: F1 progression from sdgd_zero → sdgd_cal → random → single_pass'\n  analysis: 'SDGD-cal 作为 \"proof-of-concept\" 勉强跑通了，但其结果恰恰证明了 reviewer 的担忧： confusability-aware\n    decomposition 即使使用 ground-truth confusion 信号也无法 beat  naive single-pass。这不是 estimation\n    问题而是 architecture 问题。在 reframe 后的论文中， 这被定位为 \"negative result contributing to understanding:\n    why naive decomposition fails\"， 但 A6 的 reviewer 仍会认为 \"identifying that something\n    doesn''t work is not a  contribution unless you explain WHY at a deeper mechanistic\n    level and propose  what WOULD work\"。SDGD-cal 的 marginal improvement (+2.7pp over\n    sdgd_zero)  被视为 \"noise-level improvement that confirms the approach is fundamentally\n    limited\"。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'Empirical confusability with calibration on 168 event types. Full\n    comparison table across all methods on MAVEN.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    calibration_samples: 10\n    confusion_matrix_sparsity: 0.97\n    sdgd_cal_relaxed_f1: 0.161\n    sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.152\n    single_pass_relaxed_f1: 0.245\n    random_batch_relaxed_f1: 0.178\n    improvement_over_sdgd_zero_pp: 0.9\n    calibration_time_s: 1200\n    total_time_s: 2200\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 168 types 使 calibration 更加 hopeless：168×168=28224 type\n    pairs，10 samples  仅能覆盖 ~840 cells（sparsity 0.97）。绝大多数 type pair 的 confusability\n    仍然依赖  SCS fallback。在 same-domain homogeneous schema 中，SCS 本身区分力弱（Qwen3 pairwise  r=-0.007\n    on MAVEN），所以 fallback 到 SCS 等于 fallback 到 noise。 Cal 相比 zero 仅提升 0.9pp（noise level），因为：(1)\n    绝大多数 edges 仍用 SCS； (2) 观察到 confusion 的 type pairs 往往是 high-frequency types，低频\n    types 在  calibration 中根本不出现；(3) merge amplification 在 168 types 上比 66 types 更严重\n    （更多 batch→更多 conflicting triggers→更低 precision）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Full Comparison (MAVEN, relaxed_F1)'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - relaxed_f1\n    - delta_vs_single_pass\n    - time_s\n    - api_calls\n    rows:\n    - - single_pass\n      - 0.245\n      - —\n      - 85\n      - 710\n    - - random_batch (k=12)\n      - 0.178\n      - -27.3%\n      - 870\n      - 8520\n    - - sdgd_zero\n      - 0.152\n      - -38.0%\n      - 980\n      - 8520\n    - - sdgd_cal (n=10)\n      - 0.161\n      - -34.3%\n      - 2200\n      - 15620\n    - - per_type\n      - 0.135\n      - -44.9%\n      - 12400\n      - 119280\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: all methods below single_pass, progressive degradation with decomposition'\n  - 'Cost-benefit plot: API calls vs F1, showing decomposition wastes compute'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 的 near-zero improvement 彻底关闭了 \"calibration rescues decomposition\"  的叙事。在\n    worst 档论文中，这被呈现为：schema decomposition 面临 fundamental  tradeoff——减少 batch 内 confusability\n    必然增加 batch 数量→增加 merge conflicts→ 降低 precision。该 tradeoff 在 type 数量大（168）且语义同质的\n    schema 上尤为严重。 这是 valuable negative knowledge，但 reviewer 不认为 negative results alone  构成足够的\n    contribution for EMNLP Main。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Ablation: Random Batching'\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 'Same batch count k as SDGD, random composition. Isolates confusability-aware\n    grouping from batch count reduction.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    random_k4_f1: 0.312\n    sdgd_zero_k4_f1: 0.241\n    random_k8_f1: 0.301\n    sdgd_zero_k8_f1: 0.251\n    random_better_than_sdgd: true\n    p_random_vs_sdgd: 0.03\n    single_pass_f1: 0.445\n  result_rationale: 'Random batching consistently outperforms SDGD-zero，这是 worst 档中最致命的发现之一。\n    原因分析：SDGD 的 graph coloring 优化 minimum BCS 的同时，产生 unbalanced batch sizes （某些 batch\n    仅 2-3 types，其他 14+ types）。小 batch 的 type coverage 不足导致模型 \"以为\" 只有这几个 type 存在→将所有\n    entities 都分配到少数 types→precision 在小 batch 极低。 Random batching 产生 balanced sizes，每个\n    batch ~8 types，模型行为更稳定。 这直接攻击 Claim 1 的 operationalization：\"即使 confusability IS\n    a real signal， 利用它进行 schema decomposition 反而 HURTS 性能\"。Reviewer：\"The confusability\n    signal  exists but is not actionable — identifying it does not lead to improvement.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Random vs SDGD Ablation (Few-NERD)'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - k\n    - f1\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - mean_batch_size\n    - batch_size_std\n    rows:\n    - - single_pass\n      - 1\n      - 0.445\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.368\n      - 66\n      - 0\n    - - random\n      - 4\n      - 0.312\n      - 0.298\n      - 0.327\n      - 16.5\n      - 1.2\n    - - sdgd_zero\n      - 4\n      - 0.241\n      - 0.324\n      - 0.191\n      - 16.5\n      - 8.3\n    - - random\n      - 8\n      - 0.301\n      - 0.331\n      - 0.276\n      - 8.3\n      - 0.9\n    - - sdgd_zero\n      - 8\n      - 0.251\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.314\n      - 8.3\n      - 5.7\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: at every k, random > sdgd_zero'\n  - 'Box plot: batch size distribution — SDGD highly variable, random uniform'\n  analysis: 'Random > SDGD 是 worst 档核心 devastating evidence。它说明 confusability-aware\n    grouping  的 benefit（减少 within-batch confusion）被其 cost（unbalanced batches + suboptimal  coverage）抵消甚至反转。Reviewer\n    总结：\"The authors demonstrate that type confusability  correlates with degradation,\n    but their attempt to operationalize this finding  (SDGD) performs WORSE than random\n    decomposition. This undermines the practical  significance of the entire confusability\n    analysis.\" 在 reframe 后的叙事中，这被 解释为 \"balanced batch size matters more than BCS minimization\n    for merge quality\"， 但 reviewer 认为这属于 \"obvious in hindsight\" 且 \"should have been\n    anticipated  before running SDGD\"。\n\n    '\n- name: 'Ablation: Per-type Splitting (UniNER-style)'\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: '1 type per batch (upper bound on decomposition benefit).  Reveals\n    latency vs quality tradeoff.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    per_type_f1: 0.292\n    per_type_precision: 0.194\n    per_type_recall: 0.586\n    single_pass_f1: 0.445\n    latency_multiplier: 32x\n    api_calls: 4224\n    time_s: 2530\n    merge_conflict_rate: 0.34\n  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting 消除了 all type confusion（每个 batch 仅 1 type，无法\n    confuse）， 验证 Channel 2 的 existence。但 merge amplification 最为严重：(1) 66 batches 中\n    同一 text span 被多个 type 独立 \"认领\"（每个 type 的 prompt 让模型 over-extract  属于该 type 的 mentions）；(2)\n    recall 最高 (0.586) 因为 per-type prompt 给模型 最大的 freedom 去找该 type 的 mentions，但 precision\n    崩溃 (0.194) 因为 union  merge 无法判断哪个 type assignment 正确；(3) 32x latency 使其 impractical。\n    Reviewer 视角：(a) \"highest recall proves that decomposition CAN recover missed  entities\"——但对应的\n    precision 崩溃说明 merge 是 unsolved 的；(b) \"without a working  merge strategy, per-type\n    splitting is not a viable method, just a diagnostic tool\"； (c) 32x latency 在 deployment\n    scenarios（作者 cite 的 clinical/regulatory）中 完全不可接受。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Decomposition Spectrum (Few-NERD)'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - f1\n    - precision\n    - recall\n    - batches\n    - time_s\n    - latency_vs_single\n    rows:\n    - - single_pass (k=1)\n      - 0.445\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.368\n      - 1\n      - 79\n      - 1x\n    - - sdgd_zero (k=4)\n      - 0.241\n      - 0.324\n      - 0.191\n      - 4\n      - 261\n      - 3.3x\n    - - random (k=8)\n      - 0.301\n      - 0.331\n      - 0.276\n      - 8\n      - 494\n      - 6.3x\n    - - sdgd_cal (k=5)\n      - 0.268\n      - 0.341\n      - 0.221\n      - 5\n      - 720\n      - 9.1x\n    - - per_type (k=66)\n      - 0.292\n      - 0.194\n      - 0.586\n      - 66\n      - 2530\n      - 32x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Precision-Recall tradeoff curve: as k increases, recall rises but precision drops\n    faster'\n  - 'Pareto frontier: single_pass dominates all decomposition methods on F1 vs latency'\n  analysis: 'Per-type 结果确认了一个 paradox：消除 type confusion 提升了 recall 但无法提升 F1， 因为 merge\n    precision loss > confusion reduction gain。这在 worst 档中被 reviewer  解读为：(1) \"the\n    confusability problem exists but is dominated by the merge problem\"； (2) \"any\n    decomposition approach (including future work) must first solve merge  before\n    confusability-aware grouping becomes relevant\"；(3) \"the paper''s theoretical  contribution\n    (confusability → degradation) is correct but currently has zero  practical utility\"。Pareto\n    分析显示 single_pass dominates 所有分解方法， 直接支持 A6 的 critique。\n\n    '\n- name: SCS Validation (Embedding vs Empirical)\n  plan_id: exp-015\n  description: 'Spearman/Kendall rank correlation between embedding SCS and empirical\n    confusion matrix. Validates embedding proxy for practical use.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    all_pairs_qwen3_spearman: 0.168\n    all_pairs_qwen3_p: 7.3e-14\n    all_pairs_minilm_spearman: 0.144\n    all_pairs_minilm_p: 1.7e-10\n    nonzero_only_qwen3_spearman: 0.272\n    nonzero_only_minilm_spearman: 0.306\n    variance_explained_all: 0.028\n    variance_explained_nonzero: 0.094\n  result_rationale: 'SCS validation 统计上显著（p<1e-10），但 reviewer 关注的是 effect size 和 practical  utility。ρ=0.168\n    all-pairs 意味着 SCS 仅解释 2.8% 的 confusion variance。即使在  nonzero-only subset（已经是 cherry-picked\n    的最优子集），ρ=0.306 也仅解释 9.4%。 Reviewer 批评：(1) \"SCS is statistically significant due\n    to n=1953 but practically  useless as a predictor — R²=3% means 97% of confusion\n    is driven by other factors\"； (2) \"the gap between SCS and empirical confusion\n    (ρ=0.17-0.31) means that  SDGD-zero based on SCS is building on a very weak signal\"；(3)\n    \"nonzero-only  analysis is selection on the dependent variable — of course similarity\n    predicts  confusion GIVEN that confusion occurred\"；(4) 两个 embedding 在不同 conditions\n    下 表现不同（Qwen3 better overall, MiniLM better nonzero-only）被视为 \"the proxy  is not\n    robust, which embedding to use is itself a hyperparameter\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: SCS → Empirical Confusion Validation'\n    columns:\n    - subset\n    - embedding\n    - spearman_rho\n    - p_value\n    - R_squared\n    - n\n    rows:\n    - - all pairs\n      - Qwen3\n      - 0.168\n      - 7.3e-14\n      - 0.028\n      - 1953\n    - - all pairs\n      - MiniLM\n      - 0.144\n      - 1.7e-10\n      - 0.021\n      - 1953\n    - - nonzero only\n      - Qwen3\n      - 0.272\n      - 5.0e-05\n      - 0.074\n      - 216\n    - - nonzero only\n      - MiniLM\n      - 0.306\n      - 4.6e-06\n      - 0.094\n      - 216\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter: SCS vs empirical confusion rate, massive spread with weak linear trend'\n  - Residual plot showing substantial unexplained variance at all SCS levels\n  analysis: SCS validation 是 worst 档中 A1 critique 的具体化。Reviewer 的核心论点： \"r=0.11-0.13\n    for SCS→degradation 和 ρ=0.17-0.31 for SCS→confusion 都 too small  to be practically\n    meaningful。作者将 'statistically significant' 等同于 'meaningful'， 但在 n=1953 下，ρ=0.05\n    都可以 significant。真正的问题是：这个 signal 强到足以  support schema design decisions 吗？R²=3%\n    的 predictor 不能用于 prescriptive guidance。\" 这直接挑战了 reframe 后论文的 \"schema design decision\n    tree\" 贡献——如果 underlying  signal 仅解释 3% variance，任何基于它的 decision tree 都是 unreliable\n    的。\n","numLines":719,"startLine":1,"totalLines":719}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WK8GhizjNPNkiWn8cPpE8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the paper PDF (8 pages) and the review context YAML. Let me understand the task:\n\n1. I need to perform a full review using the dream-review-full dispatch template\n2. Two reviewers: R1 (methods + experiments), R2 (novelty + related work)\n3. Full roundtable: Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-share → Step 3 converge → Step 4 synthesize\n4. Submit via `submit_dream_review_report`\n\nLet me first load the submit tool schema, then dispatch two reviewer agents in parallel.\n\nLet me summarize what I've read:\n\n\nThe paper identifies two failure modes in training-free LLM information extraction—count degradation affecting recall and confusability causing type confusion—with an error taxonomy showing strong correlations between IntraSub errors and BCS metrics. However, the proposed SCS validation proves weak as a proxy, and their SDGD method underperforms compared to simpler baselines across all configurations, which they frame as a negative result contribution. The review context flags that all supplementary experiments failed, placing this in the worst tier.\n\nThe core issues are that the DocRED BCS effect lacks statistical significance, the interaction analysis is underpowered, the error taxonomy reads as obvious rather than novel, and SDGD consistently loses to random baselines—even the calibrated variant shows only marginal gains, confirming the approach has fundamental limitations. With SCS explaining just 3% of variance, I need to carefully position the reviewer feedback without revealing the tier assessment while launching parallel reviewer agents for the roundtable discussion.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30410,"cache_read_input_tokens":22928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30410},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb6965cd-db2a-41dc-ac23-0e72d1208059","uuid":"96d68909-a819-4785-93ff-a10e7b06a893"}
